Literal case-body prose retains its authored line boundaries at every width.
The embedded words "case 1:" must remain prose rather than becoming a new arm
label. This preserves the historical formatter-closure regression without
prose filling or case-body bonds: formatting cannot insert a newline here.
TestCorpusInputsProperty also checks the re-parsed AST.
-- input.gsx --
package views

component Prose(k string) {
	<div>{ switch k {
	case "a":
		x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x case 1: nope
	default:
		<i>y</i>
	} }</div>
}
-- invoke --
Prose("a")
-- diagnostics.golden --
-- render.golden --
<div>x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x x case 1: nope</div>
